  (text "═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n           PHOTONIC AI CHIP - CONTROL & READOUT ELECTRONICS\n                 8-Channel Transimpedance Amplifier Array\n═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nARCHITECTURE:\n  PIC Outputs (8× photodiodes) → [TIA Array] → [Comparators] → USB\n\nKEY SPECIFICATIONS:\n  • Photodiode: Integrated Ge on silicon photonics chip\n    - Responsivity: 0.8 A/W @ 1550nm\n    - Capacitance: ~50 pF\n    - Dark current: ~1 µA\n\n  • TIA Configuration (per channel):\n    - Op-Amp: OPA2356 (1.4 GHz GBW)\n    - Feedback resistor: 10 MΩ (for pA-level currents)\n    - Feedback capacitor: 50 pF (compensation)\n    - Gain: Rf = 10 MΩ → 10 MV/A (10V per µA)\n    - Output range: 0 to +3.3V (single supply)\n\n  • Comparator: LM393 (dual supply: ±5V)\n    - Threshold voltage: Set by reference divider\n    - Output: Digital spike (TTL compatible)\n\n  • Phase Shifter Control:\n    - DAC: AD5684 12-bit (sets 0-3.3V for 8 channels)\n    - Driver: Op-amp buffer + MOSFET heater driver\n    - Thermo-optic phase shifter on PIC\n    - Power per shifter: ~50 mW\n\n  • USB Interface:\n    - FT2232H dual-channel USB-to-SPI/UART\n    - Control: Set DAC values, read spike data\n    - Data rate: Up to 480 Mbps (HS USB)\n\nLAYOUT NOTES:\n  ✓ Ground plane on layer 2 (critical for analog)\n  ✓ Separate AGND and DGND (star-point at USB)\n  ✓ TIA inputs shielded from digital noise\n  ✓ Phase shifter power supply clean (separate LDO if needed)\n  ✓ Thermal monitoring on each phase shifter (optional)\n\n═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n" (at 50.8 150 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (thickness 0.254))))

)
